    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear cornerstone of our offensive strategy. His score of 80.13 is the highest on the board, driven by a plus-matchup against Dobbins and an elite 10% boost from occupying the leadoff spot. We are also banking on significant production from **Yordan Alvarez** (62.19) and **Kyle Schwarber** (61.18); while **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher test in Bryan Woo, his elite 0.465 xwOBA provides the necessary floor to remain a high-end start despite the SP skill penalty. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (60.55) projects well in the three-hole, offering a solid blend of volume and park-adjusted power despite the marginal hit from facing a lefty in Rogers.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Dillon Dingler**, who narrowly missed the cutoff with a 37.83 efficiency score. While he benefits from a favorable park factor, the severe 15% penalty against the platoon dynamic against Burke, S ultimately pushed him below our 40.0 floor threshold. On the other end of the spectrum, we are closely monitoring the status of **Nelson Velazquez**, who sits right on the edge of our efficiency floor at 40.76. His inclusion is purely volume-based pending confirmation of the lineup, but he remains a high-risk play compared to the stability of **Caleb Durbin** (47.16), whose value is bolstered by the 2% SB upside provided by his favorable matchup against the slow delivery of the opposing starter.\n\nRisk management remains paramount today, particularly with **Gary Sanchez** and **Kazuma Okamoto**, both of whom are facing high-caliber arms in Skubal and Weathers, respectively. The heavy SP skill penalties (-19% and -13%) significantly dampen their ceilings. We are also navigating a lineup of \"Pending\" status for **Yordan Alvarez** and **Nelson Velazquez**; any shift in their projected batting order will necessitate an immediate re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores. While we would love to deploy **Trea Turner** or **Lars Nootbaar** to bolster our stolen base totals, their absence from the active lineup leaves us to rely on the speed-weighted projections of **Caleb Durbin** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** to carry the category.",
